# Prometheus 101 - environment
#
# Copy this file and fill in your Elastic Serverless values:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real credentials.

# --- Required -----------------------------------------------------------
# The Prometheus remote write endpoint for your Elastic Serverless project.
#
# This is superdemo's shape, copied deliberately. superdemo writes to the
# zero-segment form (utils/prometheus-grafana/grafana.yaml), which lands in
# metrics-generic.prometheus-default - so the Grafana datasource you provision
# in chapter 07 and the one superdemo provisions are the same string, and
# superdemo's "Prometheus" saved search works against your data unmodified.
ELASTIC_PROM_RW_ENDPOINT=https://your-project.es.us-east-1.aws.elastic.cloud/_prometheus/api/v1/write
#   -> metrics-generic.prometheus-default

# The explicit form routes to a data stream of your choosing. Prefer it the
# moment more than one cluster writes into one project - "generic" stops being
# a useful name at the second cluster.
# Shape: https://<host>/_prometheus/<type>/<dataset>[/<namespace>]/api/v1/write
# ELASTIC_PROM_RW_ENDPOINT=https://<host>/_prometheus/metrics/prom101/api/v1/write
#   -> metrics-prom101.prometheus-default

# API key with privileges to write via _prometheus AND to run _query.
ELASTIC_API_KEY=replace-with-your-elastic-api-key

# --- Discovered by scripts/setup.sh if you leave them unset -------------
# The Elasticsearch base URL that answers POST /_query. setup.sh probes for
# this and appends it to .env once it finds a host that works.
# ELASTIC_ES_URL=https://your-project.es.elastic.cloud

# The data stream your remote write lands in. Derived from the endpoint path
# above, then verified against the cluster once real data arrives. Set it
# explicitly here to override the derivation.
# DATA_STREAM=metrics-prom101.prometheus-default

# --- Kibana: `make links` (chapter 02 on) and `make import` (chapter 07) --
KIBANA_URL=https://your-project.kb.elastic.cloud
KIBANA_API_KEY=replace-with-your-kibana-api-key

# --- Optional: local overrides ------------------------------------------
# CLUSTER_NAME=prometheus-101
# Host ports. setup.sh shifts all four by +20000 if any is taken, and writes
# the result here.
# PROM_HOST_PORT=9090
# ROUTER_NA_HOST_PORT=9000
# ROUTER_EMEA_HOST_PORT=9001
# GRAFANA_HOST_PORT=9012
